# .cursorrules — Landing SGPT (sandrapuerto.com) Rules for AI and IDE

# 1. Architectural Guardrails (Stratum Sovereign Consumer v2.0)
- Zero host ports (`0.0.0.0` or `127.0.0.1`) may be published in `docker-compose.yml` in production.
- Always use `:latest` tags (`${NGINX_IMAGE:-nginx:latest}`) for Docker images instead of pinning specific SHA digests so the repository can operate unattended.
- Service attaches to an external Stratum network via `${STRATUM_NETWORK}` (`stratum_dmz` for perimeter DMZ or `stratum_${TENANT_ORG}_internal` for tenant island).
- Maintain dual network aliases: `landing-sgpt-web` (legacy NPM compatibility) and `stratum-app-${TENANT_ORG:-sgpt}-web` (Stratum CLI route standard).
- Execution boundaries:
  * Immutable root filesystem (`read_only: true`).
  * Volatile mounts (`tmpfs`) on `/var/cache/nginx`, `/var/run`, and `/tmp` with `nosuid,nodev,noexec`.
  * Enforce `no-new-privileges: true` and `cap_drop: [ALL]` with minimal explicit capabilities.
- Cache-Busting Invariant:
  * Whenever any CSS or JS file in `public/` is modified, `python scripts/version_assets.py` MUST be executed so `?v=<sha256>` query parameters in HTML stay synchronized.
  * CI verifies this via `python scripts/version_assets.py --check`.

# 2. Content & Naming Conventions
- Visually for users (browser `<title>`, navbar logo, footer brand): use `Sandra Puerto`.
- In metadata (`meta author`, Open Graph, Twitter Card, JSON-LD `Person.name`), `llms.txt`, `humans.txt`, `robots.txt`, and footer copyright: use full legal name `Sandra Gabriela Puerto Torres`.

